      <preface xml:id="welcome">
        <title>Welcome to You, the Student</title>
        <p><em>This website is for you.</em> I've taught mathematics for many years, and I love it. Whether you love maths, find it difficult or haven't made up your mind, you're welcome here. I want you to get the best grades you can, but even more I want you to think clearly, ask your own questions and take those skills into whatever you do next.</p>
        <p><em>Jump right in.</em> There's one sentence I hope you'll leave behind: “We haven't done that yet.” Well, let's do it now! We won't wait for a chapter about graphs before drawing a graph, or for a particular school year before exploring a useful idea. We can start wherever a question takes us.</p>
        <p><em>Full Circle Maths.</em> So much of mathematics involves moving between connected ideas and finding our way back. Multiplication and division, expanding and factorising: one direction helps us understand the other. Sometimes we discover a branch. Squaring either 2 or -2 gives 4, so working backwards from 4 gives two possible answers. Isn't that fascinating?</p>
        <p><em>Make up the question.</em> Why always begin with a question and look for the answer? Sometimes let's begin with the answer and invent our own questions. Change the conditions, test a special case, look for a general rule, draw a picture or explain your reasoning aloud. We'll learn to recognise the difference between a handy method and the mathematical principle behind it.</p>
        <p>Mathematical language is yours to use. We'll move from familiar situations and everyday words to precise ideas such as symmetry, discrete, function and inverse. Procedures and calculations matter, but so do understanding, choosing strategies, reasoning and believing that mathematics makes sense. I'll use diagrams, technology, examples and feedback to make learning manageable, helping you learn how to learn.</p>
        <p><em>I'll support you and challenge you.</em> I'll begin with what you already know, give you clear explanations, carefully chosen examples and support when you need it. As your confidence grows, I'll gradually remove that support and invite you to tackle harder, unfamiliar problems. You won't be left behind, and you won't be held back. Everyone deserves the chance to become mathematically proficient.</p>
        <p>I'll bring the opportunities and resources. You bring your imagination, curiosity and willingness to try. <em>Let's jump right in.</em></p>
        <p><em>Ronan Downes</em></p>
      </preface>

      <preface xml:id="about-the-author">
        <title>About the Author</title>
        <p>Ronan Downes is an experienced mathematics teacher who has taught in a wide range of schools and continues to work in education. He has also worked in telecommunications and has been self-employed in photography, video production and web design.</p>
        <p>His interests connect mathematics with physics, computing, data analysis and AI. His teaching draws on classroom experience, thoughtful use of technology, cognitive load theory and Universal Design for Learning. He is developing this website to make mathematics clearer, more accessible and more enjoyable for students.</p>
      </preface>
    </frontmatter>

